  <h2>Is Instabridge or RedteaGO the Right Pick</h2>
  <div class="decision-grid">
    <div class="decision-card decision-card--primary">
      <h3>Go with Instabridge if&hellip;</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You're headed somewhere with decent hotspot density and want a free-WiFi-first backup, not a primary data plan</li>
        <li>You want the bigger percentage off (20% vs 5%) and don't mind buying through the web store instead of the app</li>
        <li>You don't need calls or texts at all, just data</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="decision-card decision-card--secondary">
      <h3>Go with RedteaGO if&hellip;</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You want a plain eSIM purchase with no app-hunting or hotspot database involved</li>
        <li>You need an actual phone number for calls or texts: RedteaGO sells plans labeled "Calls/Texts Available" plus a dedicated Call & Text package; Instabridge has no calls/texts option at all</li>
        <li>You're headed somewhere rural or off the beaten path, where a community hotspot database is unlikely to have much coverage anyway</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Two Things Worth Knowing Before You Decide</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Only RedteaGO can give you a working phone number.</strong> Instabridge's eSIM plans are data-only, full stop, with no calls or texts on any plan. RedteaGO isn't a full communication provider by default either, most of its plans are also data-only, but it does sell specific plans labeled "Calls/Texts Available" and a separate Call & Text eSIM package for travelers who need to actually be reachable.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Instabridge's discount code has a catch RedteaGO's doesn't.</strong> SP20 and TRAVELESIMEXPERT only work at checkout on Instabridge's web store (store.instabridge.com/mobile-data); Instabridge's own support confirmed there's no way to enter a promo code inside the phone app. RedteaGO's RTGF946FR has no such restriction. Neither provider has a clearly confirmed refund policy once a plan activates, so don't count on getting money back from either if you change your mind.
  </p>
  <p>
    For device setup and eSIM basics that apply to both providers, see our <a href="/compatible-devices/">eSIM compatible devices</a> guide.
  </p>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <h2>Instabridge vs RedteaGO FAQ</h2>
  <div class="content-faq">
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Which is cheaper, Instabridge or RedteaGO</h3>
      <p>They're close on US and Europe regional 1GB pricing, within a cent of each other. Instabridge's global 1GB plan works out cheaper per gigabyte than RedteaGO's global 6GB bundle. Instabridge's 20% code also beats RedteaGO's 5% code by percentage.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Can I get calls and texts with either one</h3>
      <p>Only with RedteaGO, and only on plans it labels "Calls/Texts Available," plus a separate Call & Text eSIM package. Instabridge's eSIM plans are data-only with no calls or texts option on any plan.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Why would I use Instabridge instead of a normal eSIM app</h3>
      <p>Because it's not just an eSIM app. Instabridge's core product is a free database of over 20 million community-submitted WiFi hotspot passwords, and the eSIM exists as a paid backup for when free WiFi isn't available or fast enough. RedteaGO has no equivalent free-WiFi layer.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Do the discount codes work the same way on both</h3>
      <p>No. RedteaGO's RTGF946FR works anywhere in its normal checkout. Instabridge's SP20 and TRAVELESIMEXPERT only work on its web store (store.instabridge.com/mobile-data); Instabridge's own support confirmed a promo code cannot be entered inside the phone app.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

